{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:PredictedSpectra.BetaDecaySkein","@type":"LeanModule","name":"PredictedSpectra.BetaDecaySkein","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Pow.Real","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Sqrt","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":52,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.beta_decay_locality","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.beta_decay_locality","kind":"theorem","line":252,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/beta-decay-skein.lean#L252-L267","doc":"Beta decay locality: the Skein crossing change affects exactly\none generator σ_k per converting nucleon. The remaining A-1\nnucleons contribute unchanged transfer matrices. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.electronMass_from_q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.electronMass_from_q","kind":"def","line":247,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/beta-decay-skein.lean#L247-L250","doc":"The electron mass m_e = 3 · E_× · μ₀ where E_× = ½(q - q⁻¹).\nWith μ₀ = 1.6296 MeV/Skein: m_e = 3 × 0.10452 × 1.6296 ≈ 0.511 MeV. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.skeinAmplitudeAtQ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.skeinAmplitudeAtQ","kind":"def","line":242,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/beta-decay-skein.lean#L242-L245","doc":"The Skein amplitude s = q^½ - q^{-½} at q = 1.110.\nWitness: 0.10440737953277479. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.crossingEnergy_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.crossingEnergy_pos","kind":"theorem","line":237,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/beta-decay-skein.lean#L237-L240","doc":"The crossing energy is positive (q > 1 → d → u releases energy). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.crossingEnergyAtQ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.crossingEnergyAtQ","kind":"def","line":232,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/beta-decay-skein.lean#L232-L235","doc":"The crossing energy q - q⁻¹ at q = 1.110 ≈ 0.2091.\nThis is the energy released per crossing change d → u. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.beta_plus_Q_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.beta_plus_Q_pos","kind":"theorem","line":223,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/beta-decay-skein.lean#L223-L230","doc":"The Q-value sign determines decay direction: β⁻ is energetically\nallowed iff the parent action exceeds the daughter action + m_e. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.weakAsymmetry_antisymmetric","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.weakAsymmetry_antisymmetric","kind":"theorem","line":216,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/beta-decay-skein.lean#L216-L221","doc":"The weak asymmetry is antisymmetric: A(q, μ_a, μ_b) = -A(q, μ_b, μ_a). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.pair_skein_Z2_symmetry","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.pair_skein_Z2_symmetry","kind":"theorem","line":199,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/beta-decay-skein.lean#L199-L214","doc":"The Z/2 symmetry: S_ab(q⁻¹) = S_ba(q).\nExchanging q ↔ q⁻¹ swaps the role of flavours a and b. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.pairSkeinMass","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.pairSkeinMass","kind":"def","line":193,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/beta-decay-skein.lean#L193-L197","doc":"The pair Skein mass S_ab(q) = (q·μ_a + q⁻¹·μ_b)/(q^½ + q^{-½}).\nThis is the \"mass formula\" for a crossing between flavours a and b. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BetaDecaySkein","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BetaDecaySkein","kind":"def","line":185,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/beta-decay-skein.lean#L185-L187","doc":"Top-level alias matching the manifest declaration. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:beta-decay-skein","label":"def:beta-decay-skein","md":"quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/beta-decay-skein.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.beta_minus_Q_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.beta_minus_Q_pos","kind":"theorem","line":176,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/beta-decay-skein.lean#L176-L183","doc":"The Q-value of β⁻ decay is positive when the parent action exceeds\nthe daughter action plus the electron mass. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.weakAsymmetry_equal_mass","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.weakAsymmetry_equal_mass","kind":"theorem","line":169,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/beta-decay-skein.lean#L169-L174","doc":"The weak asymmetry vanishes when μ_a = μ_b. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.weakAsymmetry_classical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.weakAsymmetry_classical","kind":"theorem","line":162,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/beta-decay-skein.lean#L162-L167","doc":"The weak asymmetry vanishes at q = 1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.weakAsymmetry","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.weakAsymmetry","kind":"def","line":155,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/beta-decay-skein.lean#L155-L160","doc":"The weak asymmetry: S_ab(q) - S_ba(q) = (q - q⁻¹)(μ_a - μ_b)/(q^½ + q^⁻½).\nThis vanishes at q = 1 (no weak force in classical limit)\nand vanishes when μ_a = μ_b (no flavour asymmetry). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BetaPlusDecay.Q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BetaPlusDecay.Q","kind":"def","line":147,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/beta-decay-skein.lean#L147-L149","doc":"The Q-value: categorical action difference. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BetaPlusDecay.m_e_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BetaPlusDecay.m_e_pos","kind":"theorem","line":145,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/beta-decay-skein.lean#L145-L145","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BetaPlusDecay.m_e","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BetaPlusDecay.m_e","kind":"def","line":144,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/beta-decay-skein.lean#L144-L144","doc":"The positron mass (mirror trefoil σ(T_{2,3})); same as electron mass. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BetaPlusDecay.n_inc","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BetaPlusDecay.n_inc","kind":"theorem","line":142,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/beta-decay-skein.lean#L142-L142","doc":"The daughter has one more neutron. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BetaPlusDecay.p_dec","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BetaPlusDecay.p_dec","kind":"theorem","line":140,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/beta-decay-skein.lean#L140-L140","doc":"The daughter has one fewer proton. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BetaPlusDecay.p_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BetaPlusDecay.p_pos","kind":"theorem","line":138,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/beta-decay-skein.lean#L138-L138","doc":"The parent must have at least one proton to decay. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BetaPlusDecay.daughter","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BetaPlusDecay.daughter","kind":"def","line":136,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/beta-decay-skein.lean#L136-L136","doc":"The daughter nucleus. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BetaPlusDecay.parent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BetaPlusDecay.parent","kind":"def","line":134,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/beta-decay-skein.lean#L134-L134","doc":"The parent nucleus. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BetaPlusDecay.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BetaPlusDecay.mk","kind":"ctor","line":132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/beta-decay-skein.lean#L132-L132","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BetaPlusDecay","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BetaPlusDecay","kind":"structure","line":127,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/beta-decay-skein.lean#L127-L145","doc":"A beta-plus decay: conjugate T̄_{3,5} insertion at the converting u-quark.\nMirror of β⁻ under q ↔ q⁻¹.\n\nProduces: daughter nucleus + positron σ(T_{2,3}) + neutrino K_{0_1}. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BetaMinusDecay.Q_q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BetaMinusDecay.Q_q","kind":"def","line":121,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/beta-decay-skein.lean#L121-L125","doc":"The 𝒬_q-value: categorical action difference (NOT classical energy conservation).\n𝒬_q = S_q(parent) - S_q(daughter) - S_q(electron).\nThis differs from T_e + T_ν̄ + T_recoil by the q-anomaly δ_q. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BetaMinusDecay.skein_coefficient","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BetaMinusDecay.skein_coefficient","kind":"def","line":119,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/beta-decay-skein.lean#L119-L119","doc":"The Skein relation: q[parent] - q⁻¹[daughter] = (q^½ - q^⁻½)[L₀]. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BetaMinusDecay.m_e_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BetaMinusDecay.m_e_pos","kind":"theorem","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/beta-decay-skein.lean#L117-L117","doc":"Electron mass is positive. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BetaMinusDecay.m_e","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BetaMinusDecay.m_e","kind":"def","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/beta-decay-skein.lean#L115-L115","doc":"The electron mass (trefoil T_{2,3}). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BetaMinusDecay.n_dec","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BetaMinusDecay.n_dec","kind":"theorem","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/beta-decay-skein.lean#L113-L113","doc":"The daughter has one fewer neutron. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BetaMinusDecay.n_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BetaMinusDecay.n_pos","kind":"theorem","line":111,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/beta-decay-skein.lean#L111-L111","doc":"The parent must have at least one neutron to decay. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BetaMinusDecay.p_inc","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BetaMinusDecay.p_inc","kind":"theorem","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/beta-decay-skein.lean#L109-L109","doc":"The daughter has one more proton. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BetaMinusDecay.daughter","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BetaMinusDecay.daughter","kind":"def","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/beta-decay-skein.lean#L107-L107","doc":"The daughter nucleus. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BetaMinusDecay.parent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BetaMinusDecay.parent","kind":"def","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/beta-decay-skein.lean#L105-L105","doc":"The parent nucleus. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BetaMinusDecay.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BetaMinusDecay.mk","kind":"ctor","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/beta-decay-skein.lean#L103-L103","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BetaMinusDecay","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BetaMinusDecay","kind":"structure","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/beta-decay-skein.lean#L95-L119","doc":"A beta-minus decay: T_{3,5} insertion at the converting d-quark.\nThe 10-crossing T_{3,5} braid (σ₁σ₂)⁵ partitions into:\n- 3 crossings → electron trefoil T_{2,3}\n- 0 crossings → antineutrino unknot K_{0_1}\n- 7 crossings → nuclear re-reduction (R2 moves)\n\nProduces: daughter nucleus + electron T_{2,3} + antineutrino K_{0_1}. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.NuclearLink.A","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.NuclearLink.A","kind":"def","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/beta-decay-skein.lean#L88-L89","doc":"Mass number A = p + n. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.NuclearLink.action_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.NuclearLink.action_pos","kind":"theorem","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/beta-decay-skein.lean#L86-L86","doc":"The action is positive. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.NuclearLink.action","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.NuclearLink.action","kind":"def","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/beta-decay-skein.lean#L84-L84","doc":"The categorical action S_q evaluated on this normal form. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.NuclearLink.n","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.NuclearLink.n","kind":"def","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/beta-decay-skein.lean#L82-L82","doc":"Number of neutrons. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.NuclearLink.p","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.NuclearLink.p","kind":"def","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/beta-decay-skein.lean#L80-L80","doc":"Number of protons. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.NuclearLink.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.NuclearLink.mk","kind":"ctor","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/beta-decay-skein.lean#L78-L78","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.NuclearLink","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.NuclearLink","kind":"structure","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/beta-decay-skein.lean#L75-L86","doc":"A nuclear link configuration: proton count, neutron count, and\nthe Gröbner normal form data. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.crossing_budget_correct","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.crossing_budget_correct","kind":"theorem","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/beta-decay-skein.lean#L64-L69","doc":"The crossing budget sums correctly. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.weak_vertex_crossings","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.weak_vertex_crossings","kind":"theorem","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/beta-decay-skein.lean#L60-L62","doc":"The weak vertex has 10 crossings. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.weakVertex","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.weakVertex","kind":"def","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/beta-decay-skein.lean#L55-L58","doc":"The canonical weak vertex with its 10-crossing budget. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.WeakVertex.budget","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.WeakVertex.budget","kind":"theorem","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/beta-decay-skein.lean#L53-L53","doc":"The crossing budget is exact: 3 + 0 + 7 = 10. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.WeakVertex.reduction_crossings","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.WeakVertex.reduction_crossings","kind":"def","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/l